# ─── Samples & malware. Rule #1: no APK enters git. ────────────────────────────
# 00_GUIDING_MAP.md §4 requires this from commit #1, with an allowlist for the
# inert canary only.
*.apk
*.apks
*.xapk
*.dex
# The one APK we author ourselves. Committed as a prebuilt artifact so the demo
# does not require a Java/Gradle toolchain. Note this MUST be outside any ignored
# directory — git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded,
# which is why the artifact lives in canary/dist/ and not canary/app/build/.
!canary/dist/*.apk
!canary/dist/.gitkeep
data/samples/
# Root-anchored: bare `observations/` also matched data/fixtures/observations/, which
# holds REAL rescued ObservationArtifacts committed on purpose as regression fixtures
# (tests/contract/test_real_observation_artifacts.py). Detonation output lands on the
# sealed VM, never here, so the blanket rule bought nothing and silently excluded the
# one place observation JSON belongs.
/observations/
v1-reference/**/observations/

# ─── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*-signing.pub
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# ─── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
# Root-anchored deliberately: bare `dist/`/`build/` also match canary/dist/ and
# canary/app/build/, and an unanchored `build/` silently un-allowlists the canary.
/dist/
/build/

# ─── Corpus & ML artifacts (large / regenerable / data not code) ──────────────
*.csv
*.csv.gz
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.onnx
*.tflite
# `models/*` not `models/` — a directory pattern excludes the directory itself and
# no `!` rule can re-include anything inside it, so `!models/.gitkeep` would be dead.
#
# The shipped bundle IS tracked, by explicit decision. It is 3.8 MB total (largest
# file 2.2 MB), so it costs the clone little, and it means the model the paper cites
# travels with the commit that cites it instead of living only in a GCS bucket a
# reader cannot reach. `gs://cybershield-505518-models/` stays the runtime source.
#
# What is still excluded is everything a RUN produces — scratch bundles, sweeps,
# checkpoints — so `git status` does not fill with artefacts after every retrain.
models/*
!models/.gitkeep
!models/classifier_v1.pkl
!models/calibrator_v1.pkl
!models/anomaly_v1.pkl
!models/background_v1.npy
!models/vocab_v1.json
!models/model_card.json
!models/metrics.json
data/corpus/
androzoo_cache/

# ─── Experiment tracking (v1 left 1.7MB of mlflow state in-tree) ─────────────
mlflow.db
mlruns/

# ─── Runtime output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
.cache/
*.pcap
*.sqlite
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
data/drishti.db

# ─── Node / UI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
ui/dist/
.vite/

# ─── OS / editor litter ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ─── Terraform ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example

# Gradle (v1 left its build cache in-tree)
.gradle/
canary/local.properties
canary/app/build/
v1-reference/**/build/

# The three Android apps this repo compiles: DRISHTI Shield (the guard app), the
# inert challan decoy, and the inert benign control sample. Sources are tracked;
# build output and the SDK path are not. Their APKs are already blocked by the
# repo-wide `*.apk` rule above and are deliberately NOT allowlisted —
# `canary/dist/` remains the only committed artifact, and scripts/demo_up.sh
# rebuilds all three in well under a minute.
shield/local.properties
shield/build/
shield/app/build/
canary/decoy-challan/local.properties
canary/decoy-challan/build/
canary/decoy-challan/app/build/
canary/benign-sanchay/local.properties
canary/benign-sanchay/build/
canary/benign-sanchay/app/build/

# Runtime state written by scripts/demo_up.sh (pids, logs). Never committed.
.demo/

# Local agent worktrees. Never commit their contents.
.worktrees/

# LaTeX build spill. `docs/figures/` holds generated figures only; the paper's
# class file and architecture renders live in REPORT/ and were copied here by a
# pdflatex run from the wrong working directory.
docs/figures.zip
docs/figures/*.cls
docs/figures/sys_*.png
REPORT/*.aux
REPORT/*.log
REPORT/*.out
brand_icons/*.png
!data/kb/brand_icons/README.md
